# PRE-PLAN for Dingle's bike: "point and go". One periscope does everything: where you aim is where you drive,
# and the trigger fires the gun at the same spot. A lever is the throttle (off = coast, so you can look around).
#   engine force = cos(aim) * 100 * throttle      pump speed = -sin(aim) * 100 * throttle  (pumping out = rise)
# TO VERIFY IN GAME: the periscope's angle convention (0 = right? up = +90 or -90?). If the bike dives when you aim
# up, flip the pump multiplier ( mem Value=100 -> -100 ). Engine force +100 pushes the way the sub faces.
name bike: aim to drive, trigger to shoot
dev scope periscope 0
dev throttle switch 1
dev eng engine
dev ballast pump
dev gun turret Reload=0.25

box drive
note "POINT AND GO" "in1 = periscope angle (deg), in2 = throttle lever (0/1). out1 -> engine set_force, out2 -> pump set_speed, out3 -> turret position_in (passed straight through)"
c cx cos
c sy sin
c k mem Value=100
c kn mem Value=-100
c fx mul
c fy mul
c tx mul
c ty mul
w in1 cx.in sy.in out3
w cx.out fx.1
w k.out fx.2
w sy.out fy.1
w kn.out fy.2
w fx.out tx.1
w fy.out ty.1
w in2 tx.2 ty.2
w tx.out out1
w ty.out out2

wire scope.position_out drive.in1
wire throttle.out drive.in2
wire drive.out1 eng.set_force
wire drive.out2 ballast.set_speed
wire drive.out3 gun.position_in
wire scope.trigger_out gun.trigger_in

at 2 set scope 90         # aim straight up
at 4 set scope 180        # aim behind
at 6 toggle throttle      # throttle off: coast
at 8 toggle scope         # hold the trigger for 1 s
at 9 toggle scope
watch drive.out1 drive.out2
expect 1 eng = 100
expect 1 ballast = 0
expect 3 eng = 0
expect 3 ballast = -100
expect 5 eng = -100
expect 7 eng = 0
expect 7 ballast = 0
expect 10 gun.shots = 4
expect 10 gun.angle = 180
run 11
